  |"},{"n":114,"t":""},{"n":115,"t":"【4†Cookbook】 | 【46†Recipes】 | 【47†Ingredients】 | 【48†Equipment】 | 【49†Techniques】 | 【50†Cookbook Disambiguation Pages】 | 【51†Recipes】 | 【52†Dessert】 | 【53†Cuisine of the United Kingdom】"},{"n":116,"t":"Eton mess is a 【52†dessert】 of English origin consisting of a mixture of strawberries, pieces of meringue and cream, which is traditionally served at Eton College's annual prize-giving celebration picnic on the \"Fourth of June\" (actually celebrated on the last Wednesday in May).^{【54†[1]】}^{【55†[2]】}"},{"n":117,"t":"## Ingredients"},{"n":118,"t":""},{"n":119,"t":"[【56†edit】 | 【57†edit source】]"},{"n":120,"t":""},{"n":121,"t":"  * 4 medium-sized 【58†meringues】"},{"n":122,"t":"  * 280 【59†ml】 (1 ⅕ 【60†cup】 or 9 ½ 【61†fl oz】) 【62†double cream】"},{"n":123,"t":"  * 50 【63†g】 【64†icing sugar】"},{"n":124,"t":"  * 10 ml (1 【65†tbsp】) 【66†vanilla essence】"},{"n":125,"t":"  * 150 ml (⅗ cup or 5 fl oz) Greek 【67†yoghurt】"},{"n":126,"t":"  * 500 g (2 ⅕ cups or 1 【68†lb】 2 【69†oz】) 【70†strawberries】"},{"n":127,"t":"## Procedure"},{"n":128,"t":""},{"n":129,"t":"[【71†edit】 | 【72†edit source】]"},{"n":130,"t":""},{"n":131,"t":"  1. Rinse the strawberries, remove the tops, and cut into halves."},{"n":132,"t":"  2. Break the meringues into pieces (not too small) and place into a bowl."},{"n":133,"t":"  3. Put the double cream, vanilla essence, and icing sugar into a bowl. 【73†Whip】 until reasonably stiff."},{"n":134,"t":"  4. Combine the whipped cream, yoghurt, strawberries, and meringue, being careful not to mash the meringue into pieces that are too small."},{"n":135,"t":"  5. Serve in bowls."},{"n":136,"t":"## References"},{"n":137,"t":""},{"n":138,"t":"[【74†edit】 | 【75†edit source】]"},{"n":139,"t":"  1. 【76†↑】 【77†\"Glossary C–G\"†www.joyofbaking.com】. JoyofBaking.com. Retrieved 【78†10 July†en.wikipedia.org】 【79†2007†en.wikipedia.org】. `{{【80†cite web】}}`: Check date values in: `|accessdate=` (【81†help】)"},{"n":140,"t":"  2. 【82†↑】 【83†\"Dates 